From 0f6d9931beefb4dda5592b17b676244fb511b277 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 11:06:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/41] MAINTAINERS: add the Qualcomm QSEECOM TEE driver

Also correct the parameter count in the documentation: commands take between
two and ten parameters, the pairs after the first two being address-patch
descriptors. Four is the usual form, not the only one.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 Documentation/tee/qseecom.rst | 8 +++++---
 MAINTAINERS                   | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/tee/qseecom.rst b/Documentation/tee/qseecom.rst
index c21748050..e9655d3fc 100644
--- a/Documentation/tee/qseecom.rst
+++ b/Documentation/tee/qseecom.rst
@@ -32,9 +32,11 @@ field must be zero.
 Invoking a command
 ==================
 
-Commands take four parameters. The request header and the response share one
-buffer, the response following the request; the command payload is a separate
-allocation.
+Commands take an even number of parameters, from two to ten. The first two are
+the request and the response, which share one buffer with the response
+following the request. Each further pair is an address-patch descriptor and the
+buffer it names, up to four of them; the four-parameter form below is the usual
+one.
 
 =====  ==============  ===================================================
 param  attr            meaning
diff --git a/MAINTAINERS b/MAINTAINERS
index c8d4b913f..c0ea8fbb9 100644
--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -22080,6 +22080,13 @@ L:	linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org
 S:	Maintained
 F:	drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_qseecom.c
 
+QUALCOMM QSEECOM TEE DRIVER
+M:	Dawid Wróbel <me@dawidwrobel.com>
+L:	linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org
